# 🎯 Master Guide to k9s-style TUI Command System

**Analysis date:** August 7, 2025
**Based on:** Comprehensive analysis of k9s command system

---

## 📋 Context and Objectives

This guide explains the sophisticated k9s command system activated with the `:` key, including parsing, auto-completion, suggestions, and execution. It provides a complete blueprint for implementing a similar system in any TUI.

## 🏗️ Command System Architecture

### 1. **Activation Flow**

```
User presses ':'
     ↓
bindKeys() maps KeyColon → activateCmd()
     ↓
App.activateCmd() activates prompt
     ↓
Prompt.SetModel(cmdBuff) configures buffer
     ↓
Interface shows command line
     ↓
User types command + args
     ↓
Interpreter.grok() parses input
     ↓
Command.run() executes command
```

### 2. **Main Components**

```
k9s Command System
├── 🔤 Key Activation (internal/ui/key.go)
│   ├── KeyColon = 58 (':')
│   └── Mapping in bindKeys()
├── 📝 Command Buffer (internal/model/)
│   ├── CmdBuff - Basic text buffer
│   ├── FishBuff - Buffer with auto-suggestions
│   └── SuggestionFunc - Auto-completion function
├── 🎯 Prompt UI (internal/ui/prompt.go)
│   ├── TextView with input capture
│   ├── Keyboard handling
│   └── Display suggestions
├── 🧠 Interpreter (internal/view/cmd/interpreter.go)
│   ├── Command line parsing
│   ├── Command/argument separation
│   └── Syntax validation
├── 📚 Command Registry (internal/view/cmd/types.go)
│   ├── Special commands (quit, help, cow)
│   ├── Navigation commands (ns, ctx, dir)
│   └── Advanced commands (xray, rbac, alias)
└── ⚡ Executor (internal/view/command.go)
    ├── Command routing
    ├── Argument handling
    └── Action execution
```

## ⌨️ Key Activation and Mapping

### **Colon Key Definition**

```go
// internal/ui/key.go
const (
    KeyColon = 58  // ASCII character ':'
)

func initKeys() {
    tcell.KeyNames[KeyColon] = ":"
}
```

### **Binding in Application**

```go
// internal/ui/app.go
func (a *App) bindKeys() {
    a.actions = NewKeyActionsFromMap(KeyMap{
        KeyColon:       NewKeyAction("Cmd", a.activateCmd, false),
        tcell.KeyCtrlR: NewKeyAction("Redraw", a.redrawCmd, false),
        tcell.KeyCtrlP: NewKeyAction("Persist", a.saveCmd, false),
        // ... more bindings
    })
}

// Function that activates command mode
func (a *App) activateCmd(evt *tcell.EventKey) *tcell.EventKey {
    if a.InCmdMode() {
        return evt  // Already in command mode
    }
    a.ResetPrompt(a.cmdBuff)  // Configure prompt
    a.cmdBuff.ClearText(true) // Clear buffer
    return nil
}
```

